# Git discipline

- Keep changes scoped to the requested task.
- Do not rewrite shared history.
- Do not force-push unless explicitly requested.
- Prefer small reviewable commits or logical change groups.
- Before large changes, inspect `git status` and current branch.
- Do not commit secrets, generated credentials or local environment files.
- Call out unrelated local modifications before touching overlapping files.
- For parallel editing, use isolated worktrees/environments when edits may collide.
